`vendo completions <shell>` prints the TAB-completion script for bash, zsh or fish.
The installer saves it and sets up your shell to load it, so you rarely need to run it yourself.

Current shell could not be detected automatically.

Completions are available for bash, zsh and fish. To install them:
For bash, add this line to ~/.bash_profile:
  eval "$(vendo completions bash)"
For zsh, add these lines to the end of ~/.zshrc:
  autoload -Uz compinit && compinit
  eval "$(vendo completions zsh)"
For fish, save the script where fish loads it:
  vendo completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/vendo.fish
Then open a new terminal.
